From 838fa9a0d11633b1b91397039fc76333622a7e8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Nuttall <brandon_nuttall@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:59:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 59/59] qwen4_exp: mix LocalArgmaxMixin into the MTP draft head

Qwen4ExpMTP picks each MTP draft token by materialising full-vocab logits,
even though the repo already provides the O(2 * tp_size) path for exactly
this case: LocalArgmaxMixin builds the argmax from per-rank (value, index)
pairs instead of all-gathering a vocab-sized tensor.

The mixin needs only self.logits_processor and self.lm_head, both already
present on this class, and it is the established idiom for draft heads
(Qwen3_5MTP, the llama/qwen3 Eagle drafters, deepseek_eagle3). Wiring it in
is what makes use_local_argmax_reduction usable with this model: without
get_top_tokens the speculative-config validator refuses to start, so draft
steps keep paying a full head read per speculative step.

Measured on this host's eight serving GPUs (7x RTX 3090 + 1x RTX 3090 Ti,
TP2 x PP4, MTP K=3, 8 slots saturated, bench.py, two runs each): 8-way
aggregate decode 268-312 -> 325-346 tok/s (+10-20%), per-stream 60.5-63.5 ->
64.7-72.0 tok/s (+7-13%), event rate 101-114 -> 121-130/s. Single-stream is
unchanged-to-better at 16K context; short-context (4K) single-stream decode
lands ~8-10% lower (acceptance 2.46 vs 2.67), so the flag stays opt-in. The
repo's reference shape is four cards; this change is shape-independent (it
only makes the existing reduction usable), but the numbers are from the
eight-GPU instance.

Applied to both platform implementations (nvidia, amd) to keep them in step.
No functional change unless the flag is enabled.
Signed-off-by: Brandon Nuttall <brandon_nuttall@outlook.com>
